yahttp
------------------------------------------
YaHTTP aims to be a pure http request/response parser that has no IO ties. It
is intended to be used on small-footprint applications and other utilities that
want to use HTTP over something else than network IO.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libyahttp-devel-0.2.1-1bl3
  libyahttp0-0.2.1-1bl3
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20261107-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libboost-devel-1.66.0-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/cmouse/yahttp

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/cmouse/yahttp/archive/refs/tags/v0.2.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack yahttp-0.2.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./yahttp-0.2.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/yahttp-0.2.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/yahttp-0.2.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libyahttp0-0.2.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libyahttp-devel-0.2.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

